{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id108728188"}, "name":{"label":"mjykbus"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-09-22T03:02:29-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"3"}, "im:version":{"label":"7.0.3"}, "id":{"label":"13169427251"}, "title":{"label":"Consistently does not sync with watch"}, "content":{"label":"I have legitimately had this app for about eight or nine years now. It does a decent job of tracking steps and it’s fairly simple to use, which is nice. You literally just throw it in your pocket and off you go. It is exceedingly frustrating that this does not completely sync up with the watch for consistency unless I take my phone out and bring it to my watch. Lately, my watch is off by several thousand steps by the end of the day. Usually, I have to update the software and everything sinks up fine. This time I reinstalled iOS 26 software on both my phone and my watch, but it is not made a difference. Not a dealbreaker, especially since I’m using the free version, but frustrating nonetheless.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=712286167&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
